<title>KENYA: Regional sanctions groups to allow aid into Burundi.</title>
<headline>Regional sanctions groups to allow aid into Burundi.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A regional committee monitoring sanctions against Burundi said on Thursday it would allow the United Nations and aid agencies to import a variety of relief items into the tiny central African nation.</p>
<p>A statement issued by the committee made up of Tanzania, Kenya, Rwanda, Uganda, Ethiopia and Zambia said the decision was in response to concerns raised over the plight of displaced people in war-torn Burundi.</p>
<p>The statement said the items to cater for 250,000 internally displaced people includes food, bean seeds, water purification agents, blankets, plastic sheeting, jerry cans and buckets, cooking materials and sanitary facilities.</p>
<p>Regional countries imposed sanctions on Burundi on July 31 to punish Tutsi military leader Major Pierre Buyoya after he ousted Hutu president Sylvestre Ntibantunganya on July 25.</p>
</text>
